title: comfyui-apng-motion
message: "If you use this software or its workflows in published work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Gg22333"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Gg22333/comfyui-apng-motion"
url: "https://gg22333.github.io/comfyui-apng-motion/"
license: MIT
version: 1.3.3
date-released: "2026-11-24"
abstract: >-
  A ComfyUI skill and toolkit that turns 3-8 keyframes into coherent APNG, WebP
  and GIF animations at 8/12/24/30/60 frames. Uses latent interpolation rather
  than per-frame generation, ships ready-to-import workflows for SDXL and
  DiT-family models (MOSS-Image, FLUX, SD3, Krea, Anima), and includes a motion
  preset library, frame-timing control (fps, per-beat dwell, easing) and
  three prompt dialects (CLIP tags, Qwen-VL prose, T5 sentences).
keywords:
  - comfyui
  - apng
  - webp
  - gif
  - animation
  - latent-interpolation
  - sdxl
  - moss-image
  - prompt-engineering
  - storyboard
